WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.900
A major priority of the protest movement that's consumed Hong Kong for the past 3 and half months

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.360
is awarding the surveillance apparatus that literally everywhere.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:23.400
Demonstrators have pulled down camera poles, spray painted lenses, used green lasers to destroy sensors,

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.740
and shielded themselves with umbrellas while marching through the streets.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:39.500
There's a growing concern about surveillance and it's totally understandable,

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.160
because there's a total lack of trust in the government with this whole saga.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.540
Though Hong Kong is politically autonomous under the one country two systems model,

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:54.880
local authorities have wired up the city enabling them to keep an eye on ever corner of public life here.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:59.960
And protestors suspect they may be sharing that information with the Chinese government,

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:06.040
Hong Kong officials deny that camera's on top of the city's so-called smart lamp posts

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:10.880
feed location or facial recognition data to Beijing. But that may be a lie.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:14.340
Activists with the political organization, Demosisto,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:18.060
analyze the internal components of one of these cameras

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:23.560
and found an ethernet switch that could conceivably connect to the main land surveillance network.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.300
They also found components inside that were manufactured by a company

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.340
that's a known supplier of the Chinese government surveillance technology.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:37.340
People are becoming more and more suspicious about any kind of possible surveillance.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:40.140
Are you tracking my Bluetooth on my phone?

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.960
Are you tracking my signals?

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.300
Are you trying to get the
information about my whereabouts?

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:51.260
How could I trust that you are not doing
that? That's why we always say, okay, use VPN.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:57.300
Many times demonstrators use virtual private networks or VPNs to access the internet.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.600
And they communicate through telegram,
which fully encrypts their messages.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.220
Many of these groups in telegram are tens of thousands of people.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:09.340
And the more important thing is you can stay anonymous.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:18.260
Anonymity, particularly for this particular campaign, has become a big concern for many of these protesters.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:23.180
Without a safe communication, I don't think this revolution can last for that long actually.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:29.140
The government can crackdown everybody, very very easily, if there's no encryption in this revolution.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:35.720
Demonstrators are also refraining from using their credit cards and the digital payment system, Octopus,

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:40.840
which is an option in Hong Kong's public transit system and most stores.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:44.800
October card. Actually every single payment you make, it can be traced.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:51.460
Actually there are many, many cases that some protesters were proved that they have been to certain

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:56.180
locations, and certain times, because they
have used those Octopus cards.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:12.360
To discuss strategy demonstrators use LIHKG,

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:17.260
a social media site that allows anonymous posting and is known as the Reddit of Hong Kong.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:21.940
They've also created decentralized networks for sharing information through airdrop,

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:26.840
a function on the iPhone that transfers data directly to another person via bluetooth,

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:28.980
without a third party intermediary.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:33.400
This is a movement that is totally leaderless and decentralized,

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:41.260
and the reason for that is the youngsters, first of all, they have kick-started the whole movement

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:49.820
by using all these tools internet to really find a newer way to organize the sort of movement

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:53.320
and to really sustain it in the longer term.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.700
The protest movements, unofficial motto is "be water." A Bruce Lee phrase that's meant to convey

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:02.580
A Bruce Lee phrase that's meant to convey that in a battle, the more fluid and malleable an adversary,

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:03.760
the harder it is to stop.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:47.460
The absence of a central authority has left the protestors communication network

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.920
particularly vulnerable to sabotage.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:55.800
Twitter recently removed what they said were approximately 200,000 Chinese state-linked accounts,

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:00.400
spreading rumors of protest violence being orchestrated by foreign powers.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.980
Fake news is a big, big problem in Hong Kong.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:34.740
I'm working with some people in journalism, and academic areas to try to see

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:39.380
that there are more locally based fact checking organizations that can be set up.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:43.080
And I think that would go a long way.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:48.620
A major factor motivating the protestors in their fight to maintain political autonomy from mainland China

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:53.560
is the surveillance apparatus that the Beijing government imposes on its own citizens.

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:58.640
Such as the social credit system in which individuals are rated for good behavior,

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:05.800
and a bad score can impede their ability to travel, attend the best schools, or get hired for the best jobs.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:11.820
We worry so much about surveillance, facial recognition everywhere, social credit, the great firewall.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:17.160
To average people in Hong Kong, do you expect these things to be extended to Hong Kong in 10 years time?

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:22.380
I think most people cannot answer that question with confidence to say that it will not.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.060
And that is the problem.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:03.420
The Hong Kong government has stopped answering the demands of the protestors.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:06.660
And the conflict grew more acrimonious on October 1st

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:12.140
after a police officer shot in the chest and injured an 18 year old demonstrator who had attempted to hit him

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:13.240
with a rod.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:17.400
Last week, the government announced a ban on wearing face masks in the street.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:25.000
It has escalated to a point where people are realizing what we need is a political reform

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:28.120
in the whole Hong Kong legislative system.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:32.060
And also of course, that the communist
government is not backing down either.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:38.500
So we are preparing ourselves for an even longer fight.

